{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","title":"lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3523,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","line":6067,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The $B$-gradient is orthogonal to the kernel of the functional]\n\\label{lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker}\n\n\\uses{def:bilinear-gradient}\n\n\n\n\nWith the preceding notation, $a^\\sharp\\in(\\ker a)^\\perp$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:bilinear-gradient}\n\\sketch For $w\\in\\ker a$, symmetry and Definition \\ref{def:bilinear-gradient} give $B(w,a^\\sharp)=B(a^\\sharp,w)=a(w)=0$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B$\">$B$</span>-gradient is orthogonal to the kernel of the functional] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a62696c696e6561722d6772616469656e742d6f7274686f676f6e616c2d6b6572\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Abilinear-gradient\">↗ def:bilinear-gradient</a> <p></p>With the preceding notation, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a^\\sharp \\in (\\ker a)^\\perp $\">$a^\\sharp \\in (\\ker a)^\\perp $</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Abilinear-gradient\">↗ def:bilinear-gradient</a> \\sketch For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w\\in \\ker a$\">$w\\in \\ker a$</span>, symmetry and Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Abilinear-gradient\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a62696c696e6561722d6772616469656e74\">17</a> give <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B(w,a^\\sharp )=B(a^\\sharp ,w)=a(w)=0$\">$B(w,a^\\sharp )=B(a^\\sharp ,w)=a(w)=0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient","title":"def:bilinear-gradient","label":"def:bilinear-gradient"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","title":"prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","label":"prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:embedding-criterion-nondegenerate-pointwise","title":"lem:embedding-criterion-nondegenerate-pointwise","label":"lem:embedding-criterion-nondegenerate-pointwise"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","title":"lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[The $B$-gradient is orthogonal to the kernel of the functional]\n\\label{lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker}\n\n\\use